<http://data.silknow.org/object/08d2aee8-e4db-3d2d-a4cc-f79e5d797400/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Sumpter tapestry hanging. Woven in wool and silk on a woollen warp. Decorated with ten naked and winged boys flanking baskets of flowers and fruit, the four largest baskets are angled into the corners, on a yellow ground. The spaces are filled with brightly polychrome acanthus stems, fruit and flowers. Boys and baskets cast dark red shadows. All four borders face outwards.\n\nThe border design, with scrolling blue acanthus stems as background to small spread eagles in the corners and griffins with foliate trails supporting swags of flowers on each side, a version of a wider border with coat-of-arms hiding the griffins' tails."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/08d2aee8-e4db-3d2d-a4cc-f79e5d797400> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/08d2aee8-e4db-3d2d-a4cc-f79e5d797400/dimension/4>
